39,2,1,talk,Mio,,"Wow, the transport costs are huge when we go far! Also, whole-building lets are risky because if someone cancels, the rest of us have to pay. We should be really careful about that!","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"It seems we must be mindful of how we choose our lodging. I have learned that members bond most when they sleep in the same place, though some unfortunately do not attend away camps at all.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"The administrative side of public facilities is a nightmare. The application is tedious and the lottery system is far too rigid. Also, staying on campus means we'd have to cook for ourselves, which is a huge burden.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,1,talk,Rin,,"@Ryuji, that sounds awful! I found out that staying on campus means our training would be split into weird early or late hours. Plus, the inland places have eight people to a room and strict lights out! That's not relaxing at all.","{""words"":42,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,1,talk,Misaki,,"I've found that public beds are quite affordable at 1,100 yen. However, a third of our members can't reach campus by 9 AM without overnight lodging, which adds hidden costs to a local camp.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Mio,,"@Misaki, that's a great point about the hidden costs! If we stay local, we might still be paying for beds. But @Ryuji, if the public booking is such a nightmare, maybe we should avoid those?","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Misaki"",""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"It is a difficult balance. While public facilities may be a burden to organize, we must remember that sharing a living space is what truly brings our different year-groups together. We should not lose that.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Shizue, I understand the value of bonding, but we cannot ignore the cost of labor. A nine-page application and a lottery system are inefficient. We need a destination that doesn't burn out the organizers.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,2,talk,Rin,,"@Shizue, but if we're all squeezed eight to a room with a strict curfew, people will be grumpy, not bonding! We need a place where we can actually rest so we have energy to be friends!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"If we avoid public facilities to save Ryuji from paperwork, we must be careful. A private lodge might seem easier, but as Mio mentioned, the non-refundable deposits for cancellations could create another budget gap.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Ryuji"",""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Mio,,"@Misaki, exactly! It's scary to think we'd have to cover someone else's cost. But if we stay on campus, we're splitting our training times and cooking for ourselves, which sounds like a mess!","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"It seems the campus option may be too disruptive for our training and our spirits. Perhaps a place where we can all stay together, but without such rigid rules, would be the kindest choice for everyone.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Shizue, I agree that campus is problematic. Between the cooking duty and the fragmented schedule, it's not viable. However, the public centers are equally unattractive due to the administrative burden and the rigid lottery.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,3,talk,Rin,,"@Ryuji, @Shizue, if campus is a mess and public centers are too strict and hard to book, maybe the lodge is best? As long as we can sleep well and not be grumpy!","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Ryuji"",""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,3,talk,Misaki,,"The lodge is an option, but we must be cautious. If we choose it, we need a strict policy on cancellations to ensure the club account doesn't end up covering the deficit again.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Mio,,"I agree with Misaki! If we go with the lodge, we need a clear rule about cancellations so no one gets stuck with a surprise bill. It sounds like the best way to keep everyone happy and rested!","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,2,4,talk,Shizue,,"If we can ensure the financial arrangements are fair and clear, the lodge seems like a wonderful way to encourage our members to bond and feel at home together.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,"The lodge avoids the administrative nightmare of public bookings and the labor of cooking on campus. If we can resolve the cancellation risks Misaki mentioned, it is the most rational choice for the organizers.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,2,4,talk,Rin,,Yay! I'm so glad we all agree! A lodge sounds like the most fun and the best place to get some real sleep. Let's go for it!,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,2,4,talk,Misaki,,"I agree. The lodge avoids the administrative burden and the scheduling conflicts of the other options. As long as we establish a firm payment policy for cancellations, it is the most viable choice.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
